\begin{align*}
a + (a+d) + (a+2d) + (a+3d) + (a+4d) &= 70\\
(a+9d) + (a+10d) + (a+11d) + (a+12d) + (a+13d) + (a+14d) + (a+15d) + (a+16d) + (a+17d) + (a+18d) &= 210
\end{align*}
Simplifying these equations, we get:
\begin{align*}
5a + 10d &= 70\\
19a + 95d &= 210
\end{align*}
From the first equation, we can solve for $a$ in terms of $d$. We get:
\begin{align*}
5a &= 70 - 10d\\
a &= 14 - 2d
\end{align*}
Substituting this expression for $a$ into the second equation, we get:
